It is a beautiful Saturday morning.
I leave the flat and go outside.
Then I get on the bicycle.
Today I am not riding to the office.
I have decided to help in a community café on Saturdays.
The café is run by a local association.
During the week I always work on the laptop.
I want to meet people who do not work in the tech industry.
That is why I am now learning to work in a café.
I ride through the quiet streets.
The spring sun is shining and it is pleasantly warm.
I am already quite excited.
And I am also a little nervous.
This is my first shift today!
I have never made coffee for guests before.
But I am really looking forward to this new experience.
I will be there in five minutes.
